## Foreach
`foreach` loops through every element in a collection without needing an index:

```csharp
string[] items = {"Sword", "Shield", "Potion"};
foreach (string item in items) {
    Console.WriteLine(item);
}
```

Compare with `for`:
```csharp
// for - you manage the index
for (int i = 0; i < items.Length; i++) {
    Console.WriteLine(items[i]);
}

// foreach - cleaner, no index needed
foreach (string item in items) {
    Console.WriteLine(item);
}
```

Use `foreach` when you don't need the index. Use `for` when you do.

